# VibeGridNative Usage Guide

## Overview
VibeGridNative is a high-performance universal cell renderer for TanStack Table with 42.54ms render performance. It uses a single optimized component to handle all cell types with meta-based configuration.

**NEW**: Now supports generated columns from @repo/dataforge with easy column selection!

## Key Files
- Main component: [VibeGridNative.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/custom/vibegridnative/components/VibeGridNative.tsx)
- Usage example: [VibeGridNativeUsageExample.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/custom/vibegridnative/examples/VibeGridNativeUsageExample.tsx)
- Generated columns: [column-configurations.ts](mdc:packages/dataforge/src/generated/column-configurations.ts)

## 🏭 Generated Columns Approach (RECOMMENDED)

The easiest way to use VibeGridNative is with generated columns from @repo/dataforge:

### Import Generated Columns
```tsx
import { VibeGridNative, type RelationshipDataProvider } from '@/components/custom/vibegridnative/components/VibeGridNative'
import { TaskColumns, TaskStatusOptions, TaskPriorityOptions } from '@repo/dataforge/column-configurations'
import type { Task } from '@repo/dataforge/client-entities'
```

### Column Selection
```tsx
// Define which columns to display (in order)
const SELECTED_COLUMNS: (keyof Task)[] = [
  'title',        // Core business field
  'status',       // Enum with business logic
  'priority',     // Enum with permissions  
  'project',      // Relationship (many-to-one)
  'assignee',     // Relationship (many-to-one)
  'dueDate',      // Date field
  'description',  // Text field
  'tags',         // Additional text field
  'id',           // System field (read-only)
  'createdAt'     // System field (read-only)
]

// Generate column array from selected columns
const columns: ColumnDef<Task>[] = SELECTED_COLUMNS.map(columnKey => {
  const column = TaskColumns[columnKey]
  if (!column) {
    throw new Error(`Column ${columnKey} not found in TaskColumns`)
  }
  return column
})
```

### Benefits of Generated Columns
✅ **Full Business Logic**: Includes permissions, audit logging, allowed transitions  
✅ **Complete Enums**: All enum values and labels pre-configured  
✅ **Relationships**: Proper relationship configuration with display fields  
✅ **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript support from generated types  
✅ **Zero Configuration**: Just select which columns to show  
✅ **Easy Updates**: Column changes automatically picked up from schema  

