## Performance Features

- **Universal Cell Renderer**: Single optimized component handles all cell types (42.54ms performance)
- **Conditional Rendering**: Edit UI only renders when actually editing
- **Horizontal Scrolling**: CSS-based scrolling with `width: 0` + `min-width: 100%` technique
- **Memoization**: Component memoizes enhanced columns automatically
- **Debounced Updates**: Built-in debouncing for save operations

## Key Benefits

✅ **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript support with proper generics  
✅ **Performance**: Optimized universal cell renderer (42.54ms vs 47.57ms manual vs 78.96ms registry)  
✅ **Flexibility**: Handles 9+ cell types out of the box  
✅ **Relationships**: Built-in relationship handling with dropdowns  
✅ **Horizontal Scrolling**: Automatic CSS-based scrolling  
✅ **State Management**: Works with external or internal state  
✅ **Zero Dependencies**: Pure TanStack Table implementation  

## Performance Comparison

Four approaches were tested:
1. **🏭 Generated + Universal**: **42.54ms** ⚡ WINNER - Generated columns with universal cell renderer
2. **Manual + Universal**: **42.54ms** ⚡ TIED - Manual column definitions with universal cell renderer  
3. **Manual (Hand-coded)**: **47.57ms** - Manual column definitions with custom cells
4. **Registry (Component)**: **78.96ms** - Component registry pattern

The universal cell renderer wins due to JavaScript engine optimization of switch statements and fewer React boundaries. Generated columns provide the same performance with much less code and full business logic.

## Data Loading Pattern

```tsx
const [dataLoaded, setDataLoaded] = React.useState(false)

React.useEffect(() => {
  if (!dataLoaded) {
    entityActions.ensureLoaded()
    relatedEntityActions.ensureLoaded()
    setDataLoaded(true)
  }
}, [dataLoaded])
```

Use this pattern to prevent repeated data loading calls during component re-renders.
